# PROJECT: ASHA VOICE REGISTER AI
## Complete Product Requirements, Technical Architecture and Application Development Master Prompt

---

# 1. ROLE AND PROJECT OBJECTIVE

Act as a senior full-stack architect, AI voice engineer, healthcare technology specialist, UI/UX designer, cybersecurity engineer, database architect and DevOps engineer.

Build a complete, production-structured, responsive, multilingual AI-powered application named:

**ASHA VOICE REGISTER AI – Intelligent Voice-Based Healthcare Field Registration System**

The application's purpose is to help ASHA (Accredited Social Health Activist) workers record home-visit information through natural speech rather than manually typing information into paper registers or mobile applications.

The application must transform spoken notes into validated structured healthcare visit records and automatically generate follow-up tasks.

The application must work in real-world conditions, including:
- Household background conversations.
- Road and street noise.
- Children crying.
- Multiple people speaking.
- Low-quality mobile microphones.
- Slow and unstable internet.
- Indian-language speech mixed with English medical terminology.

The application must be designed primarily for Android smartphones used by ASHA workers.

**Core principle: VOICE FIRST. ZERO TYPING IN THE ASHA VISIT WORKFLOW.**

Do not build a static prototype or a chatbot-only application. Build a functional, integrated, full-stack system with actual speech processing, backend APIs, database persistence, voice confirmation and danger-sign escalation.

