# 6. AUTOMATIC FOLLOW-UP MANAGEMENT

After a visit is saved, automatically generate a follow-up action list.

Example:

VISIT COMPLETED

Beneficiary: Nandini
Visit type: ANC

NEXT ACTIONS:
- Follow-up visit on the date confirmed by the worker.
- Track the reported ANC follow-up status.
- Review the recorded vaccination status.
- Check any pending actions.
- Refer immediately if an approved danger-sign event was recorded.

Newborn example:

- Schedule the next home visit using the configured, approved schedule.
- Check immunisation follow-up.
- Review previously recorded measurements.
- Track incomplete visit actions.
- Maintain referral follow-up status.

The application must distinguish:

- Routine follow-up.
- Pending information.
- Scheduled visit.
- High-priority referral.
- Immediate referral.

Generate dates only from explicitly supplied dates or approved, versioned schedule rules.

If necessary information is missing, ask the ASHA worker.

Do not invent follow-up dates.

